            <ArticleTitle>Antinociceptive activity of the natural piperidine alkaloid hydrochlorides from Syphocampylus verticellatus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In addition to 3'-methoxyluteolin and mixtures of sterols and triterpenes, the leaves of Syphocampylus Verticellatus yielded two piperidine alkaloid hydrochlorides, one of them has a novel structure. The alkaloids exhibit antinociceptive activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
